note: Steady state: each bucket is sized as if its rate held, with no scale-up lag. A fleet that follows the plan must start replicas one start time before the rate arrives.
note: Each bucket is sized for the p95 of its cycles' rates. A p95 needs 20 cycles in the bucket; with fewer the bucket is sized for its mean, which is less conservative (FewCyclesForP95).
note: Needed is the fewest replicas whose fleet limit, at the SLO and headroom 0.85, reaches the rate: the fewest in all, ties to fewer decode (POST /v1/size's search, whatifapi.SmallestFleet). Another mix may serve the rate too. The fleet the bucket had is judged as one fleet at the same rate: under when its limit falls short, over when one replica fewer of either role would still serve it.
note: An hour's need, and the peak, is a fleet that holds every sized bucket in it, priced again at each bucket's rate and shape: the fewest of the buckets' own fleets that holds them all, else each role's most over them. It is not searched for the fewest: a smaller mix may hold them too. The busiest bucket's own fleet is given beside it (busiest); it need not hold a bucket of a lower rate but longer requests.
note: A bucket with fewer than 30 requests is not sized (too little data); a bucket no cycle fell in has no data.
note: Had is the median serving pods of the priced prefill and decode variants over the bucket's cycles; the rate is the model's. A bucket in which another variant also served is flagged OtherVariantsServed. The prefix hit rate is reported, not priced.
note: Where prefill is not priced, decode is sized on its own limit alone: a lower bound (at least). The fleet's limit, which decode admission can hold down, is not priced.
